📘 DFDL – Logical Structure (Short Notes)

🔹 Meaning:

Logical Structure = DFDL modeling ka pehla step.

Isme tu data ko logical blocks (groups & fields) me todta hai.

Focus: structure samajhna, annotations (like separator, length) baad me aate hai.



---

🔹 Key Concepts:

Concept	Meaning

Complex Structure	Record / group of related fields (e.g., one employee record).
Simple Item	Single field (e.g., name, age, salary).
Ordering	Fields ka order — fixed (sequence) ya alternative (choice).
Cardinality	Field repeat hoga kitni baar (1, 0..1, n times, unlimited).
Nillable / Default	Jab value missing ho, kya karna hai (allow null / default).
Reuse	Common fields ko global types banao (e.g., name, age).



---

🔹 Example: Employee Data

John,25,1999-01-01,Y,50000
Raj,30,1994-02-02,N
Ana,28,1996-03-03,Y,45000

Step	Description

1️⃣ Complex Structures	Root → employees, Repeating group → employeeRecord
2️⃣ Simple Items	name, age, dob, permanent, salary
3️⃣ Ordering	All in fixed order → sequence
4️⃣ Cardinality	employeeRecord → unbounded, salary → optional
5️⃣ Nillable / Default	salary missing → minOccurs=0, numeric field → nillable=true (if needed)
6️⃣ Reuse	name, age → reusable simple/global types



---

🔹 Logical Schema Snippet

<xs:element name="employees">
  <xs:complexType>
    <xs:sequence>
      <xs:element name="employeeRecord" maxOccurs="unbounded">
        <xs:sequence>
          <xs:element name="name" type="xs:string"/>
          <xs:element name="age" type="xs:int"/>
          <xs:element name="dob" type="xs:date"/>
          <xs:element name="permanent" type="xs:boolean"/>
          <xs:element name="salary" type="xs:decimal" minOccurs="0"/>
        </xs:sequence>
      </xs:element>
    </xs:sequence>
  </xs:complexType>
</xs:element>


---

🔹 Bottom Line:

Logical Structure = define what data looks like.

Annotations (next step) = define how to parse it (e.g., separator, terminator, encoding).



---

Bhai bole toh —
Logical step = structure sochna,
Annotation step = parsing rule likhna. ✅


